WEBVTT

00:07.070 --> 00:10.900
Tokyo

00:30.760 --> 00:31.670
Tsubasa!

00:32.170 --> 00:35.800
Be careful, and don't stray too far away!

00:37.390 --> 00:42.680
As long as he's got a football, he's all happy!

00:42.680 --> 00:43.890
He sure is!

00:54.450 --> 00:58.700
Tsubasa will already be two years old
by the time I get back from the ocean.

00:58.700 --> 01:01.370
Make sure he doesn't forget about you!

01:02.500 --> 01:04.710
He won't cry this time.

01:06.790 --> 01:08.250
Hey, where's Tsubasa?

01:08.250 --> 01:10.170
Wasn't he over there just now?

01:10.170 --> 01:13.130
He's in danger if he gets too
close to the road by himself!

01:13.130 --> 01:14.420
Tsubasa!

01:24.430 --> 01:25.850
Tsubasa!

01:31.360 --> 01:32.400
Tsubasa!

01:51.090 --> 01:56.680
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:51.090 --> 01:56.680
<i>koronde toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:56.680 --> 02:01.350
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:56.680 --> 02:01.350
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

02:02.600 --> 02:07.270
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

02:02.600 --> 02:07.270
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

02:08.140 --> 02:15.860
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

02:08.140 --> 02:15.860
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

02:15.860 --> 02:21.620
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

02:15.860 --> 02:21.620
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

02:21.620 --> 02:30.380
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

02:21.620 --> 02:30.380
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:30.380 --> 02:35.920
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:30.380 --> 02:35.920
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:35.920 --> 02:41.850
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:35.920 --> 02:41.850
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:41.850 --> 02:43.510
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:43.510 --> 02:50.730
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:43.510 --> 02:50.730
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:50.730 --> 02:53.730
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Go, our kicks!</i>

02:50.730 --> 02:53.730
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kick o</i>

02:53.730 --> 02:58.150
<i>Leap out into a huge TV</i>

02:53.730 --> 02:58.150
<i>tobidasô dodekai TV</i>

03:09.500 --> 03:14.090
<b>Episode 1: Take Off!</b>

03:14.460 --> 03:17.460
Sign: -10 years later, in the Pacific Ocean-

03:29.560 --> 03:30.980
Is that your son?

03:30.980 --> 03:32.020
Yeah.

03:32.020 --> 03:33.900
He's name is Tsubasa.

03:33.900 --> 03:35.400
Oh, yeah?

03:35.400 --> 03:40.740
But he's not on a football field in that picture.
Why is he posing with a jersey?

03:40.740 --> 03:42.570
He's moving today.

03:42.570 --> 03:43.240
What?

03:43.240 --> 03:46.030
He's marking his arrival
at a new home ground.

03:46.030 --> 03:47.700
I see.

03:47.700 --> 03:53.420
Having said that, I doubt he'll be much help at home.

03:54.250 --> 03:58.760
Sign: Nankatsu, Shizuoka Prefecture

03:59.420 --> 04:01.170
Thank you for helping!

04:01.170 --> 04:02.470
You're welcome!

04:02.470 --> 04:05.510
Tsubasa, where are you?

04:05.510 --> 04:07.220
Come here and give us a hand!

04:17.980 --> 04:20.110
I'm going down to town for a quick look, Mother!

04:20.570 --> 04:23.780
Huh? Wait, Tsubasa!

04:25.740 --> 04:27.580
Hey, you!

04:27.580 --> 04:31.540
Jeez, I just <i>knew</i> he'd skip out!

04:31.540 --> 04:34.290
Your son's got the right touch for football!

04:34.290 --> 04:39.050
Yeah, and it's thanks to his football that he's still alive!

04:40.590 --> 04:44.800
He's grown up together with his football!

04:45.840 --> 04:48.010
<i>That really was a miracle!</i>

04:51.060 --> 04:51.770
<i>Tsubasa!</i>

05:03.860 --> 05:04.910
<i>Tsubasa!</i>

05:06.110 --> 05:08.120
<i>When that car crashed into him,</i>

05:08.660 --> 05:10.740
<i>and when he collided against the pavement,</i>

05:11.160 --> 05:13.500
<i>the ball served as a cushion</i>

05:13.500 --> 05:16.880
<i>and Tsubasa came out of it unscathed.</i>

05:20.710 --> 05:23.250
<i>Since then, he's always been playing football.</i>

05:24.550 --> 05:26.090
It's Mount Fuji!

05:26.090 --> 05:31.390
<i>It's like he was born
to dedicate his life for football.</i>

05:36.230 --> 05:38.150
<i>This is my new town!</i>

05:53.580 --> 05:54.620
Hello!

06:03.760 --> 06:05.010
Excuse me!

06:06.380 --> 06:08.010
Oh, that's fine.

06:13.180 --> 06:15.770
Sign: Nankatsu Ginza trading street

06:24.070 --> 06:27.610
Sign: Nankatsu Public Primary School

06:28.070 --> 06:29.910
So this is where the Nankatsu school is.

06:30.780 --> 06:32.580
I wonder where Shutetsu is?

06:47.630 --> 06:49.470
It's a football field!

06:54.430 --> 06:58.190
Hey Ishizaki, will you explain why you've

06:58.190 --> 07:00.940
brought these middle school students here?

07:00.940 --> 07:02.020
What?!

07:02.020 --> 07:04.650
During our last match, as we promised,

07:04.650 --> 07:08.030
we beat you, Nankatsu, by ten goals.

07:08.030 --> 07:10.610
Therefore, as we agreed,
this field now belongs to Shutetsu.

07:10.610 --> 07:11.700
Zip it!

07:11.700 --> 07:14.580
You guys have your own field already!

07:14.580 --> 07:16.240
Go there!

07:16.240 --> 07:19.870
Us becoming national champions brought a lot of people to the club.

07:19.870 --> 07:23.130
The main field belongs to the A team.

07:23.660 --> 07:26.130
This field belongs to the B team.

07:26.130 --> 07:29.130
To the B team?!

07:29.130 --> 07:30.840
Hey, Wakabayashi!

07:30.840 --> 07:34.010
Don't get a big head just
because you're good at football!

07:35.100 --> 07:37.390
This is our underclassmen's precious field.

07:37.390 --> 07:39.600
Give it up without arguing!

07:39.600 --> 07:41.100
Captain...

07:41.100 --> 07:45.270
We can't let 'em have it this easily.

07:46.020 --> 07:48.690
But arguing about this would be a waste of my time.

07:49.400 --> 07:52.950
So, how about a challenge?

07:52.950 --> 07:54.320
You want to challenge us?

07:54.320 --> 07:55.160
Huh?

07:56.030 --> 07:57.120
That's right!

07:57.120 --> 08:00.790
All club captains will make a shot.

08:01.870 --> 08:05.090
Rugby, handball... The sport doesn't matter.

08:06.000 --> 08:08.380
Come at me with the sport you're good at!

08:15.050 --> 08:20.270
I'm sure I'll be able to stop all attempts from outside the penalty area!

08:20.270 --> 08:21.810
If you want this field,

08:21.810 --> 08:24.730
try to score a goal at me!

08:25.270 --> 08:26.690
Just what's with this guy?!

08:29.320 --> 08:32.820
If you can score even one goal, you've won.

08:35.320 --> 08:37.660
What a jerk!

08:37.660 --> 08:39.830
Don't get too full of yourself!

08:39.830 --> 08:41.120
We're in!

08:41.120 --> 08:45.420
Wakabayashi, not even a prodigy keeper like you

08:46.540 --> 08:50.340
can possibly win this challenge!

08:51.720 --> 08:54.050
We don't know before we've tried!

08:58.810 --> 09:00.970
I'm up first.

09:00.970 --> 09:03.980
Watch carefully, Ishizaki.
I'll settle this right away.

09:03.980 --> 09:05.560
I'm counting on you, sempai!

09:11.030 --> 09:12.820
Here it comes!

09:19.240 --> 09:25.040
How about that?! Unlike a football, a rugby ball bounces unpredictably!

09:32.260 --> 09:34.300
You did it, captain!

09:34.300 --> 09:37.300
Great save, captain!

09:37.300 --> 09:39.010
First one down.

09:41.600 --> 09:44.480
All right, next up is handball.

09:44.480 --> 09:48.270
A football goal is twice as large as a handball goal!

09:48.270 --> 09:50.270
If I can't score now,

09:51.270 --> 09:54.530
I'll be an embarrassment to my sport!

09:56.700 --> 09:57.360
It can't be!

09:57.360 --> 09:58.320
Incredible!

10:00.990 --> 10:04.330
As you'd expect from the prodigy keeper Wakabayashi!

10:04.330 --> 10:06.410
He's not bragging without reason!

10:06.410 --> 10:10.250
But we can't give up this field that our underclassmen hold so dearly!

10:11.840 --> 10:13.380
I'm up next!

10:13.380 --> 10:15.260
Please do it, sempai!

10:17.050 --> 10:20.550
Even <i>you</i> won't be able to stop me!

10:20.550 --> 10:24.060
If I can't score this, I'll drop out of the baseball club!

10:26.230 --> 10:27.140
Come!

10:29.980 --> 10:32.400
Why are you smiling like that?!

10:32.400 --> 10:33.150
Come at me!

10:33.150 --> 10:34.820
Don't freak out!

10:34.820 --> 10:37.610
Throw a straight fastball at him!

10:37.610 --> 10:38.410
All right!

10:40.030 --> 10:41.580
You're done for...

10:42.280 --> 10:43.740
...with this!

10:47.620 --> 10:49.920
How'd he stop that?

10:55.460 --> 10:57.630
He's a monster...

10:58.930 --> 11:00.390
Who's up next?

11:12.520 --> 11:13.770
Amazing!

11:15.230 --> 11:17.280
What's wrong? Is that all?

11:18.990 --> 11:20.740
It would seem so.

11:20.740 --> 11:22.780
I'm the last one left!

11:27.330 --> 11:30.210
What do you intend to shoot, Mr. Athlete?

11:30.210 --> 11:31.000
Hmpf.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.250
This.

11:33.210 --> 11:36.460
A javelin? That's dangerous, sempai!

11:36.460 --> 11:40.260
Don't worry, the tip's covered up, so he'll be fine.

11:40.260 --> 11:43.090
Whatever is fine by me.

11:43.090 --> 11:45.010
This guy stinks of arrogance!

11:48.100 --> 11:50.020
You think you can stop this?

11:50.850 --> 11:52.020
Throw it!

12:08.160 --> 12:09.160
He jumped!

12:12.080 --> 12:14.540
He deflected it with a kick!

12:19.260 --> 12:20.630
I can't believe this..

12:22.800 --> 12:24.390
It's settled.

12:26.010 --> 12:27.680
Train hard!

12:27.680 --> 12:29.350
Y-Yes!

12:35.810 --> 12:39.900
I've never seen a goalkeeper this amazing before!

12:46.280 --> 12:47.370
Sempai?!

12:47.910 --> 12:49.870
Sorry, Ishizaki.

12:50.790 --> 12:52.750
We've got to train, too.

12:52.750 --> 12:53.250
What?

12:53.250 --> 12:55.160
Sorry, give up on this field!

12:55.160 --> 12:59.800
Eh, what? Didn't you say to leave this to you?!

13:00.670 --> 13:03.760
Jeez, these sempai can't be trusted!

13:03.760 --> 13:05.010
Ishizaki!

13:05.010 --> 13:05.890
Huh?

13:05.890 --> 13:07.600
Didn't you hear what he said?

13:07.600 --> 13:10.140
It's time for us to train now.

13:11.890 --> 13:12.980
Damn it!

13:13.730 --> 13:15.940
Jeez, quit showing off like that!

13:15.940 --> 13:18.020
We didn't lose against <i>you</i>!

13:20.650 --> 13:21.610
Huh?

13:23.320 --> 13:26.110
Hey, where did the goalkeeper go?

13:26.110 --> 13:29.530
No idea, he surely went back to his place.

13:29.530 --> 13:31.750
Then tell me where he lives.

13:31.750 --> 13:33.750
And what will you do knowing that?

13:34.540 --> 13:35.920
I want to challenge him!

13:35.920 --> 13:37.500
Challenge him?!

13:37.500 --> 13:41.510
Are you stupid or something?
Didn't you see him in action just now?

13:41.510 --> 13:43.050
Even a baseball didn't...

13:43.050 --> 13:44.340
CHALL-ENGE!

13:46.180 --> 13:49.600
All right, I guess I'm just showing you where he lives.

13:49.600 --> 13:50.720
Thank you!

13:51.930 --> 13:54.600
What's your name?

13:54.600 --> 13:56.980
I'm Ryo Ishizaki.

13:57.270 --> 13:59.650
I'm Tsubasa Ozora!

14:18.880 --> 14:19.790
Hey, you...

14:21.040 --> 14:23.960
Why are you dribbling all the time?

14:23.960 --> 14:24.920
I love it.

14:24.920 --> 14:25.800
The ball?

14:27.050 --> 14:30.180
No, football! Don't you?

14:30.180 --> 14:32.560
Of course I love it too!

14:35.180 --> 14:38.060
<i>He's surprisingly good.</i>

14:47.860 --> 14:51.870
So you just moved here?

14:51.870 --> 14:54.490
You can see the whole town from here!

14:54.490 --> 14:55.830
Nice place, isn't it?

14:55.830 --> 14:56.910
Sure is!

14:56.910 --> 14:58.160
Look over there.

14:59.000 --> 15:01.460
Wakabayashi lives in that big house.

15:02.170 --> 15:04.590
Oh yeah? Got it!

15:04.590 --> 15:08.180
His family's been a big name in this town for a while.

15:10.970 --> 15:12.140
Hey, what're you up to?

15:23.770 --> 15:25.030
What you think?

15:25.030 --> 15:25.650
Eh?

15:26.110 --> 15:29.400
You saw it too didn't you, Wakabayashi's house?

15:30.410 --> 15:33.240
You want to challenge him too, don't you?

15:33.240 --> 15:36.660
You're... What? Are you talking to the ball?

15:36.660 --> 15:39.370
It's a good thing we moved to this town.

15:39.370 --> 15:42.040
I've got a feeling we'll experience great things!

15:43.170 --> 15:47.260
I'll be able to live out my passion for football in this town.

15:47.260 --> 15:50.300
U-Uh... Ozora...

15:50.300 --> 15:51.510
"Tsubasa"'s fine.

15:51.510 --> 15:52.760
Got it.

15:52.760 --> 15:54.180
Anyway, Tsubasa,

15:54.640 --> 15:56.810
I don't know what you're up to,

15:56.810 --> 16:00.440
but there's no way a runt like you can beat Wakabayashi.

16:00.440 --> 16:06.480
He won the national tournament
with a clean sheet.

16:06.480 --> 16:08.070
Besides, he...

16:09.820 --> 16:12.910
Hey, you! Are you even listening to me?!

16:13.870 --> 16:16.120
What are you doing now?!

16:16.120 --> 16:16.870
Huh?

16:17.870 --> 16:19.040
This will do!

16:19.790 --> 16:21.750
What's that?

16:36.510 --> 16:38.720
Hey, you serious now?

16:38.720 --> 16:42.390
You think you can shoot this ball
all the way over to Wakabayashi?

16:44.060 --> 16:46.570
Here I go!

16:54.570 --> 16:55.700
Off you go!

16:56.490 --> 16:58.330
<i>Go!</i>

17:06.920 --> 17:07.750
That's...

17:07.750 --> 17:08.420
...crazy!

17:14.930 --> 17:16.550
What's the matter, Genzo?

17:19.140 --> 17:20.720
Where did that ball come from?

17:20.720 --> 17:22.270
Mikami-san...

17:22.270 --> 17:25.900
It flew in all of a sudden from that hill.

17:25.900 --> 17:26.810
What?

17:26.810 --> 17:28.730
Don't make things up.

17:28.730 --> 17:31.530
That's way too far.

17:31.530 --> 17:32.490
But...

17:34.240 --> 17:38.700
Sign: Challenge from Tsubasa Ozora

17:36.110 --> 17:38.370
<i>"Tsubasa Ozora"...</i>

17:39.620 --> 17:43.160
A-Amazing! It reached its destination!

17:43.160 --> 17:45.120
I hope he'll accept!

17:45.120 --> 17:46.420
You're amazing!

17:46.420 --> 17:47.290
Ouch!

17:47.290 --> 17:49.340
You've got an incredibly strong kick!

17:49.340 --> 17:51.210
How'd you make it fly that far?

17:52.170 --> 17:54.380
Do you have something hidden there?

17:54.380 --> 17:56.430
I don't have anything hidden!

17:56.430 --> 17:57.180
Anyway!

17:57.180 --> 18:00.430
You actually have a chance at
beating Wakabayashi!

18:00.430 --> 18:04.060
He'll definitely accept your challenge and show up!

18:05.190 --> 18:07.900
Sign: Challenge from Tsubasa Ozora

18:07.190 --> 18:07.900
Genzo!

18:07.900 --> 18:11.820
Your vision's playing games with you. There's no way it came from there.

18:17.490 --> 18:19.740
Someone, call that doggie and make it stop!

18:19.740 --> 18:20.530
Stop, John!

18:28.290 --> 18:29.250
That was close...

18:29.250 --> 18:30.340
Who are you?

18:30.340 --> 18:31.880
He's suspicious, I'm calling the police!

18:31.880 --> 18:33.170
Ah, hold your horses!

18:33.170 --> 18:34.800
I'm not someone suspicious!

18:35.260 --> 18:42.180
I just got here by following the ball
that came flying from that hill.

18:43.270 --> 18:45.730
That means the ball really...

18:45.730 --> 18:49.730
What's more, it was shot by a kid like me.

18:49.730 --> 18:50.900
A kid, you say?

18:51.480 --> 18:54.530
Does this look like the writing of an adult?

18:58.530 --> 18:59.660
For you!

18:59.660 --> 19:01.030
Thanks!

19:01.030 --> 19:04.120
You'd better beat Wakabayashi,

19:04.120 --> 19:05.950
in the name of this ice lolly!

19:05.950 --> 19:06.710
Sure!

19:10.750 --> 19:13.040
When you challenge him, could you say

19:14.000 --> 19:21.090
that if you beat him, then Nankatsu would be allowed to use the football field again?

19:21.090 --> 19:22.260
Why?

19:22.260 --> 19:23.970
Why, you ask?!

19:23.970 --> 19:28.440
You watched the challenge between Wakabayashi and our sempai's, didn't you?

19:28.440 --> 19:29.480
I did but,

19:29.940 --> 19:33.270
there's no way I'm saying something like that. That field has two goals.

19:33.270 --> 19:35.730
Couldn't you just share it?

19:38.360 --> 19:40.200
<i>Tsubasa Ozora...</i>

19:40.200 --> 19:42.280
<i>What kind of guy is he?</i>

19:42.280 --> 19:44.740
<i>He shot the ball from that hill...</i>

19:45.540 --> 19:49.080
<i>If he's challenging me, it means he's with Nankatsu.</i>

19:49.750 --> 19:50.670
<i>No...</i>

19:50.670 --> 19:54.790
<i>Nobody in that disaster of a club
can shoot a ball anywhere near that hard.</i>

19:57.880 --> 19:59.220
<i>Hold on...</i>

19:59.220 --> 20:04.050
<i>There's no way a primary school student my age can kick a ball like that. </i>

20:04.050 --> 20:05.060
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

20:05.060 --> 20:08.810
<i> Even if his writing sucks, he's got to be either in middle school or high school. </i>

20:09.850 --> 20:10.770
Mikami-san!

20:12.060 --> 20:14.060
Is something the matter, Mikami-san?

20:14.060 --> 20:15.110
Well...

20:15.110 --> 20:18.570
I feel like I've seen that man somewhere before.

20:18.570 --> 20:20.570
That drunkard?

20:23.870 --> 20:24.620
Look!

20:24.620 --> 20:27.080
Here's the field from before.

20:27.080 --> 20:28.120
Okay!

20:28.790 --> 20:30.000
Of course.

20:30.000 --> 20:33.630
No child can shoot from that far.

20:33.630 --> 20:36.710
Even for you it'd be too hard, Genzo.

20:36.710 --> 20:37.710
You're right.

20:40.970 --> 20:42.430
It's Wakabayashi!

20:42.430 --> 20:43.260
Look!

20:43.260 --> 20:44.890
He's holding the ball!

20:44.890 --> 20:46.890
He's received my challenge!

20:50.230 --> 20:53.140
Hey Wakabashi, listen close now!

20:53.140 --> 20:56.480
He's the one who challenged you!

20:56.480 --> 20:57.860
Come again?

20:57.860 --> 20:59.990
That little boy?

21:03.990 --> 21:05.820
Nonsense!

21:05.820 --> 21:09.330
There's no way a squirt like that
has a strong enough kick!

21:09.330 --> 21:11.540
And yet he does.

21:11.540 --> 21:14.250
I saw it with my own eyes!

21:14.250 --> 21:15.460
Very well!

21:17.500 --> 21:21.420
Let's find out right now if he really is the one!

21:22.380 --> 21:24.010
Take this!

21:25.340 --> 21:27.100
That's dangerous! Dodge it!

21:32.480 --> 21:35.440
<i>He deflected my shot!</i>

21:40.280 --> 21:41.030
You!

21:42.780 --> 21:44.780
Stop! You'll hit the bus!

21:59.460 --> 22:00.920
Wakabayashi-kun!

22:00.920 --> 22:03.300
Take on my challenge!

22:06.510 --> 22:07.470
You really are...

22:08.090 --> 22:09.550
Tsubasa Ozora!

22:10.180 --> 22:14.060
That's right! I'm Tsubasa Ozora!

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
